  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Having a sense of purpose and a feeling of momentum in achieving our career goals is powerful - so when we can assist employees in getting there, it's a meaningful way to make a difference in their lives and their professional success. [This article](<HBR_How_to_Help_an_Employee_Figure_Out_Their_Career_Goals>) offers three strategies managers can use to help those who are unsure of their career path: 1) help them analyze patterns, 2) expand their worldview, and 3) don't steer too hard.",
